.TH TED 1 "November 2026" "ted 0.8.8" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
ted \- minimal zero-dependency terminal text editor
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B ted
.RI [ OPTION ]...
.RI [ FILE ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B ted
is a lightweight, zero-dependency terminal text editor written in C99 using raw
.BR termios (3)
input and ANSI escape sequences. If
.I FILE
is specified,
.B ted
opens it for editing (or initializes a new named buffer if
.I FILE
does not exist yet); otherwise, it starts with an empty buffer and displays a centered ASCII splash banner until text is entered.
.PP
Features include multi-language syntax highlighting (C/C++, Python, Shell/Bash, Makefile, Rust, Go, and Zig) with automatic
.B #!
shebang detection, matching bracket and parenthesis highlighting, incremental search, visual text selection with range clipboard operations, an atomic undo/redo command stack, smart auto-indentation after opening braces, single-line and multi-line block indentation/outdentation, line duplication and cut/paste, XTerm SGR mouse click/drag/wheel support, a dynamic line-number gutter, runtime configuration via
.IR ~/.tedrc ,
and live terminal window resizing via
.BR SIGWINCH .
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-c " FILE" "\fR, \fP" \-\-config " FILE"
Load runtime configuration from
.I FILE
instead of the default search path.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Display a usage summary and keybinding reference, then exit.
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-version
Output version information and exit.
.TP
.B \-\-
Terminate option parsing. Useful when opening a file whose name begins with
.BR \- .
.SH KEYBINDINGS & MOUSE
.SS File & Application Control
.TP
.B Ctrl-S
Save the current buffer to disk. Prompts for a filename if the buffer has not been named yet.
.TP
.B Ctrl-R
Reload the active configuration file
.RI ( ~/.tedrc ,
.IR $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/ted/tedrc ,
or the path supplied to
.BR \-\-config )
and re-render all open rows immediately.
.TP
.B Ctrl-Q
Quit
.BR ted .
If the buffer contains unsaved changes, pressing
.B Ctrl-Q
the configured number of times (default: 2 additional presses) is required to discard modifications and exit.
.SS Search, Navigation & Selection
.TP
.B Ctrl-F
Enter incremental search mode. Type a query to jump to matches in real time; use
.B Up / Left
and
.B Down / Right
arrow keys to cycle backward and forward through matches,
.B Enter
to confirm the jump, or
.B Esc
to cancel and restore the original cursor and scroll position.
.TP
.B Ctrl-G
Prompt for a 1-based line number and jump directly to that line, centering it vertically in the viewport.
.TP
.B Arrow Keys
Move the cursor one character or line at a time, wrapping across line boundaries at the start and end of lines. Clears any active visual selection.
.TP
.B Shift+Arrow Keys
Start or extend a visual selection character-by-character or line-by-line, highlighting the selected range in reverse video.
.TP
.B Esc
Clear the current visual selection.
.TP
.B Ctrl-Left / Ctrl-Right
Jump backward or forward by one word.
.TP
.B Home / End
Move the cursor to the beginning or end of the current line.
.TP
.B Page Up / Page Down
Scroll the viewport up or down by one full screen height.
.TP
.B Mouse Left-Click, Drag & Scroll Wheel
Click anywhere inside the editor viewport to position the cursor and set a selection anchor, drag with the left mouse button held to highlight a visual selection across rows and columns, or use the scroll wheel to scroll vertically by 3 lines per tick via XTerm SGR mouse reporting.
.SS Editing, Clipboard, Indentation & History
.TP
.B Ctrl-Z
Undo the last character insertion, deletion, word deletion, line split, line join, line duplication, line cut/paste, block indent/outdent, or range cut/paste.
.TP
.B Ctrl-Y
Redo the most recently undone edit.
.TP
.B Ctrl-C
Copy the active visual selection into the internal clipboard.
.TP
.B Ctrl-X
Cut the active visual selection into the internal clipboard and delete the selected range from the buffer.
.TP
.B Ctrl-V
Paste the internal clipboard contents at the cursor (replacing any active visual selection, or inserting below the current line if the clipboard holds a full line cut via
.BR Ctrl-K ).
.TP
.B Enter
Insert a newline (replacing any active visual selection first). When
.B auto_indent
is enabled, preserves the current line's leading indentation and adds an extra
.B tab_stop
indent level if the line ends with
.BR { .
.TP
.B Tab
When a multi-line visual selection is active, indent every line in the selected block by
.B tab_stop
spaces; otherwise, insert spaces up to the next
.B tab_stop
column boundary.
.TP
.B Shift-Tab
When a multi-line visual selection is active, outdent every line in the selected block by up to
.B tab_stop
leading spaces (or one leading tab); otherwise, outdent the current line.
.TP
.B Ctrl-D
Duplicate the current line directly below the cursor.
.TP
.B Ctrl-K
Cut the current line into the internal clipboard and remove it from the buffer.
.TP
.B Ctrl-U
Paste a cut line from the internal clipboard directly below the current line.
.TP
.B Backspace
Delete the active visual selection if one exists; otherwise, delete the character before the cursor or merge the current line onto the end of the previous line when at column 1.
.TP
.B Ctrl-Backspace / Ctrl-H
Delete the active visual selection if one exists; otherwise, delete the previous word (or delimiter run) before the cursor.
.TP
.B Delete
Delete the active visual selection if one exists; otherwise, delete the character under the cursor.
.SH CONFIGURATION
At startup (and when pressing
.BR Ctrl-R ),
.B ted
looks for a plain-text
.B key = value
configuration file in the following order unless overridden with
.BR \-c / \-\-config :
.IP 1. 4
.I ~/.tedrc
.IP 2. 4
.I $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/ted/tedrc
(or
.I ~/.config/ted/tedrc
if
.B XDG_CONFIG_HOME
is unset)
.PP
Blank lines and comments starting with
.B #
or
.B ;
are ignored. Booleans accept
.BR true / false ,
.BR yes / no ,
.BR on / off ,
or
.BR 1 / 0 .
Color keys accept standard ANSI SGR codes
.RB ( 30 \(en 37 ", " 90 \(en 97 )
or color names
.RB ( black ", " red ", " green ", " yellow ", " blue ", " magenta ", " cyan ", " white ", " gray ).
.TP
.BI tab_stop " = 4"
Tab stop width in columns (integer,
.BR 1 \(en 16 ).
.TP
.BI auto_indent " = true"
Enable automatic indentation on
.B Enter
(boolean).
.TP
.BI line_numbers " = true"
Display the left-hand line-number gutter (boolean).
.TP
.BI quit_times " = 2"
Extra
.B Ctrl-Q
confirmations required when quitting with unsaved changes (integer,
.BR 0 \(en 10 ).
.TP
.BI color_comment " = 36"
Syntax color for single-line and multi-line comments (default: cyan).
.TP
.BI color_keyword " = 33"
Syntax color for control-flow keywords and preprocessor/compiler directives (default: yellow).
.TP
.BI color_type " = 32"
Syntax color for built-in types, constants, and special variables (default: green).
.TP
.BI color_string " = 35"
Syntax color for string and character literals (default: magenta).
.TP
.BI color_number " = 31"
Syntax color for numeric literals (default: red).
.TP
.BI color_match " = 34"
Highlight color for incremental search matches (default: blue).
.TP
.BI color_gutter " = 90"
Color for line numbers and
.B ~
empty-row markers (default: gray).
.SH SYNTAX & BRACKET HIGHLIGHTING
.B ted
automatically detects the language from the file's basename or extension:
.TP
.B C / C++
.BR .c ", " .h ", " .cpp ", " .hpp ", " .cc
.TP
.B Python
.BR .py ", " .pyw
(including multi-line
.B """
docstrings)
.TP
.B Shell / Bash
.BR .sh ", " .bash ", " .zsh
.TP
.B Makefile
.BR Makefile ", " makefile ", " GNUmakefile ", " .mk
.TP
.B Rust
.B .rs
.TP
.B Go
.B .go
.TP
.B Zig
.B .zig
.PP
For extensionless files,
.B ted
also inspects the first line for a
.B #!
shebang (such as
.BR "#!/usr/bin/env python3" ,
.BR "#!/bin/bash" ,
.BR "#!/bin/zsh" ,
or
.BR "#!/bin/sh" )
and applies the corresponding Python or Shell syntax rules automatically.
.PP
Whenever the cursor rests on a delimiter
.RB ( ( ", " ) ", " [ ", " ] ", " { ", or " } )
outside of strings and comments,
.B ted
highlights both the delimiter under the cursor and its matching partner in bold reverse video.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.tedrc
Default per-user configuration file.
.TP
.I $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/ted/tedrc
Fallback XDG configuration path (defaults to
.IR ~/.config/ted/tedrc ).
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Normal exit via
.BR Ctrl-Q ,
.BR \-\-help ,
or
.BR \-\-version .
.TP
.B 1
An invalid command-line option was passed, the target path is a directory or inaccessible, or a fatal terminal or file I/O error occurred.
.SH AUTHOR
Written by k!M (pizslacker).
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR vi (1),
.BR nano (1),
.BR termios (3)